1
00:00:01,083 --> 00:00:04,458
The guy I was just with is my boyfriend.

2
00:00:04,583 --> 00:00:06,125
I won't tell a soul.

3
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:07,500
Don't worry.

4
00:00:08,208 --> 00:00:09,833
I finally said it out loud.

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,833
What's wrong with being a kid?

6
00:00:13,958 --> 00:00:16,458
You have plenty of time to grow up.

7
00:00:20,042 --> 00:00:22,417
I felt so lonely.

8
00:00:23,750 --> 00:00:26,792
Sorry, that got a little heavy.

9
00:00:28,042 --> 00:00:29,682
I'll cherish you for the rest of my life.

10
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:43,583
What is his deal?

11
00:00:52,458 --> 00:00:54,708
Seriously, what is that guy's deal?

12
00:00:56,167 --> 00:00:57,583
This is getting ridiculous.

13
00:00:57,708 --> 00:00:59,792
Calling people in the
middle of the night...

14
00:01:01,208 --> 00:01:03,292
Leaving the room a total mess...

15
00:01:03,667 --> 00:01:04,667
Get 'em! Go, go!

16
00:01:04,708 --> 00:01:06,792
And blasting his video
games at full volume!

17
00:01:14,208 --> 00:01:16,417
Sounds like you're having
a rough time, Harutora.

18
00:01:20,333 --> 00:01:22,708
Sorry. I know you're studying for exams.

19
00:01:22,833 --> 00:01:25,333
Don't be. You can stay as long as you want.

20
00:01:26,875 --> 00:01:30,583
If I keep coming over like this,
won't people start talking again?

21
00:01:30,708 --> 00:01:32,542
You mean the others?

22
00:01:33,375 --> 00:01:37,458
It's fine. You used to be
my roommate anyway.

23
00:01:39,583 --> 00:01:40,667
Yeah...

24
00:01:40,792 --> 00:01:43,292
I hope we can tell the
people around us someday.

25
00:01:44,292 --> 00:01:46,333
It's just, right now, I'm still a little...

26
00:01:48,583 --> 00:01:49,917
It's okay.

27
00:01:50,917 --> 00:01:53,708
Besides, we still have this, right?

28
00:01:54,417 --> 00:01:56,542
Stop it, that's so embarrassing.

29
00:01:56,667 --> 00:01:59,750
Then how about we come
up with a different signal?

30
00:02:00,458 --> 00:02:01,750
Huh?

31
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:08,200
How about something like this?

32
00:02:09,458 --> 00:02:10,625
Or maybe...

33
00:02:11,250 --> 00:02:12,500
Something like this?

34
00:02:15,958 --> 00:02:20,042
Sorry. I couldn't hide my feelings.
It's written all over my face.

35
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:22,408
I love you so much.

36
00:02:24,167 --> 00:02:26,792
All right, let me think of one too.

37
00:02:28,417 --> 00:02:31,417
Actually, no. I'll find another way.

38
00:02:31,542 --> 00:02:32,542
Huh?

39
00:02:33,750 --> 00:02:38,458
Because no matter what,
I want to room with you again.

40
00:02:46,750 --> 00:02:48,208
[Aoba Dormitory]

41
00:02:48,375 --> 00:02:50,167
Roommates again starting today?

42
00:02:50,542 --> 00:02:51,833
Yep.

43
00:02:54,125 --> 00:02:55,125
Well...

44
00:02:55,167 --> 00:02:58,125
I showed the housing office the evidence,

45
00:02:58,250 --> 00:02:59,625
and they approved it right away.

46
00:02:59,750 --> 00:03:00,958
Wait, really?

47
00:03:04,417 --> 00:03:05,875
Oh...

48
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:07,333
Wait...

49
00:03:13,208 --> 00:03:14,958
Then... what about Naruse?

50
00:03:17,042 --> 00:03:18,625
I talked him into swapping.

51
00:03:18,833 --> 00:03:19,833
Seriously?

52
00:03:21,958 --> 00:03:26,417
Turns out they're both huge gamers.

53
00:03:26,542 --> 00:03:27,750
Gamers?

54
00:03:27,875 --> 00:03:32,125
Yeah, they're obsessed
with the exact same game.

55
00:03:32,250 --> 00:03:35,917
They hit it off instantly.

56
00:03:37,375 --> 00:03:38,833
No way.

57
00:03:38,958 --> 00:03:41,375
Yes way.

58
00:03:50,083 --> 00:03:51,417
Senpai...

59
00:03:54,208 --> 00:03:56,375
Say "welcome home" to me.

60
00:03:58,875 --> 00:03:59,875
What?

61
00:04:03,708 --> 00:04:07,750
I love hearing you say
"Welcome home, Harutora."

62
00:04:15,035 --> 00:04:16,993
"Welcome home, Harutora."

63
00:04:21,417 --> 00:04:23,792
I'm home, Senpai.

64
00:05:13,292 --> 00:05:16,208
"Hold on, Harutora-kun"
(Episode 7)

65
00:05:17,833 --> 00:05:19,208
A parent-teacher conference?

66
00:05:20,208 --> 00:05:24,000
Yeah, next week, to discuss college plans.

67
00:05:24,750 --> 00:05:26,792
That really makes you feel like a senior.

68
00:05:26,917 --> 00:05:29,583
Before that, we've got Sports Day.

69
00:05:32,167 --> 00:05:36,167
Is your mom coming, by the way?

70
00:05:36,292 --> 00:05:37,667
Or your dad?

71
00:05:38,208 --> 00:05:41,000
My mom. She's really excited about it.

72
00:05:41,125 --> 00:05:42,125
I see.

73
00:05:42,250 --> 00:05:43,770
Then I should definitely go say hello.

74
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:49,292
Wait, I can't. I've got club practice.

75
00:05:49,958 --> 00:05:51,292
Right, makes sense.

76
00:05:51,417 --> 00:05:53,167
Next time, then.

77
00:05:53,667 --> 00:05:54,917
Sure.

78
00:06:08,833 --> 00:06:11,167
Why did I just feel relieved...?

79
00:06:19,208 --> 00:06:20,208
[Coming out]

80
00:06:20,250 --> 00:06:21,958
[Broke my parents' hearts]

81
00:06:22,083 --> 00:06:25,458
[They didn't understand]

82
00:06:33,167 --> 00:06:34,893
All right, the race
is in the final stretch!

83
00:06:34,917 --> 00:06:37,125
The lead pack is picking up speed!

84
00:06:37,250 --> 00:06:38,476
And someone's breaking away from the pack!

85
00:06:38,500 --> 00:06:39,893
He's like a blue streak of lightning!

86
00:06:39,917 --> 00:06:42,101
The sophomore anchor from the
basketball team, Kurobe Harutora!

87
00:06:42,125 --> 00:06:44,500
So fast! He's not slowing
down around the curve at all!

88
00:06:44,625 --> 00:06:46,333
He's accelerating down the final stretch!

89
00:06:46,458 --> 00:06:48,792
He's pulling away! A massive lead!

90
00:06:48,917 --> 00:06:51,375
He crosses the line in first place!

91
00:06:53,417 --> 00:06:55,167
Awesome, Harutora!

92
00:07:10,125 --> 00:07:12,125
Man, Harutora is crazy fast.

93
00:07:12,250 --> 00:07:13,750
Oh, hey, Sui.

94
00:07:15,417 --> 00:07:17,375
I've gotta go. I'm on first aid duty.

95
00:07:18,458 --> 00:07:20,542
What's he being so sneaky about?

96
00:07:32,542 --> 00:07:33,917
Ah...

97
00:07:34,042 --> 00:07:35,625
Did you make that yourself?

98
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,583
Is it for your girlfriend?

99
00:07:37,708 --> 00:07:42,292
Idiot, not everyone's into girls.

100
00:07:42,583 --> 00:07:44,083
Huh?

101
00:07:59,333 --> 00:08:00,708
Excuse me...

102
00:08:02,500 --> 00:08:04,333
I took a nasty fall.

103
00:08:05,583 --> 00:08:07,458
That's quite a scrape.

104
00:08:08,250 --> 00:08:10,208
Let's rinse it with water first.

105
00:08:10,333 --> 00:08:11,667
Okay.

106
00:08:11,792 --> 00:08:12,917
Ishii.

107
00:08:13,333 --> 00:08:16,458
Ishii, can you give me a hand?

108
00:08:17,333 --> 00:08:18,542
What's wrong?

109
00:08:18,667 --> 00:08:21,042
I can't stand blood...

110
00:08:23,208 --> 00:08:24,958
I'm sorry.

111
00:08:25,083 --> 00:08:28,208
It's okay, don't worry about it.
Everyone has things they can't handle.

112
00:08:30,333 --> 00:08:32,083
Hold on, let me check it out first.

113
00:08:32,208 --> 00:08:33,208
Okay.

114
00:08:33,292 --> 00:08:34,500
All right.

115
00:08:35,208 --> 00:08:37,292
Let's see... In that case...

116
00:08:41,875 --> 00:08:43,125
All done.

117
00:08:43,583 --> 00:08:44,667
Thank you.

118
00:08:44,792 --> 00:08:45,458
Take care.

119
00:08:45,583 --> 00:08:46,625
Will do.

120
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:48,625
Be careful out there.

121
00:08:48,750 --> 00:08:50,000
Okay.

122
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:57,167
Thanks.

123
00:09:02,167 --> 00:09:03,458
Um...

124
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:05,000
I'm sorry.

125
00:09:05,833 --> 00:09:07,458
It's fine, really.

126
00:09:07,583 --> 00:09:08,833
Not just about this.

127
00:09:09,167 --> 00:09:12,833
I talked behind your back
in the dorm kitchen before.

128
00:09:15,917 --> 00:09:20,042
After that, Harutora chewed me out.

129
00:09:20,917 --> 00:09:22,167
He did?

130
00:09:23,208 --> 00:09:24,250
Harutora.

131
00:09:24,375 --> 00:09:25,583
Yeah?

132
00:09:25,833 --> 00:09:27,792
Aren't you rooming with a gay guy?

133
00:09:27,917 --> 00:09:30,077
Doesn't that bother you?
Like, what if he hits on you?

134
00:09:33,417 --> 00:09:34,708
Hey.

135
00:09:35,167 --> 00:09:37,333
The person I like is a guy too.

136
00:09:39,542 --> 00:09:41,417
So cut it out.

137
00:09:45,333 --> 00:09:48,542
Kishida-senpai is a really great guy.

138
00:09:50,167 --> 00:09:53,250
That was the first time I realized

139
00:09:53,375 --> 00:09:57,542
how little respect I had
for people who are different from me.

140
00:10:00,125 --> 00:10:02,917
I'm truly sorry.

141
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,042
It's okay. Don't worry about it.

142
00:10:08,208 --> 00:10:11,333
Harutora's a really great guy, isn't he?

143
00:10:11,875 --> 00:10:15,000
Right? Don't you think so too, Ishii?

144
00:10:15,250 --> 00:10:16,500
Yeah.

145
00:10:19,042 --> 00:10:20,167
Ishii.

146
00:10:21,167 --> 00:10:23,250
Tsuchiya hurt his foot.

147
00:10:23,375 --> 00:10:25,042
Can you go patch him up?

148
00:10:25,167 --> 00:10:27,000
Right, on it...

149
00:10:29,250 --> 00:10:32,042
Is he okay? I'll come too.

150
00:10:37,250 --> 00:10:38,500
Wait...

151
00:10:46,542 --> 00:10:48,917
It's just a scrape.

152
00:10:52,542 --> 00:10:57,000
You two looked like you were having fun,
so I came to crash the party.

153
00:11:38,542 --> 00:11:41,292
Harutora... Stop.
Not out in the open like this...

154
00:11:47,167 --> 00:11:49,750
Did he say anything rude to you?

155
00:11:51,917 --> 00:11:54,625
If anything happens,
you have to tell me. I'll—.

156
00:11:57,792 --> 00:11:59,917
All right, just answer your message.

157
00:12:06,208 --> 00:12:07,750
[Kurobe Aya: Are you enjoying
track and field day? Send me photos!]

158
00:12:07,875 --> 00:12:09,292
It's from my parents.

159
00:12:14,583 --> 00:12:17,167
Wait, did you send them a picture of me?

160
00:12:17,292 --> 00:12:18,667
Yeah.

161
00:12:23,083 --> 00:12:24,250
What's wrong?

162
00:12:24,667 --> 00:12:26,000
Nothing.

163
00:12:27,083 --> 00:12:30,542
You've seemed a bit down lately, Sui.

164
00:12:31,417 --> 00:12:32,667
Huh?

165
00:12:32,792 --> 00:12:35,875
Like when we were talking about
the parent-teacher conference.

166
00:12:37,708 --> 00:12:39,833
Is something on your mind?

167
00:12:41,458 --> 00:12:42,625
Is it about college?

168
00:12:43,292 --> 00:12:46,875
Ah, well...

169
00:12:57,708 --> 00:12:59,708
Harutora, your parents...

170
00:13:01,625 --> 00:13:04,333
if they found out you had a boyfriend...

171
00:13:05,042 --> 00:13:07,083
how do you think they'd react?

172
00:13:10,083 --> 00:13:11,167
Hmm.

173
00:13:12,333 --> 00:13:15,625
They just went, "Got it! Congratulations!"

174
00:13:15,750 --> 00:13:17,542
Pretty much like that.

175
00:13:18,083 --> 00:13:19,083
Wait...

176
00:13:21,542 --> 00:13:22,667
You already told them?

177
00:13:22,792 --> 00:13:23,917
Yeah.

178
00:13:24,583 --> 00:13:27,833
My mom called and asked me
out of nowhere the other day.

179
00:13:28,792 --> 00:13:30,750
She just asked you straight out?

180
00:13:32,708 --> 00:13:35,917
She'd been watching some
drama about a gay couple,

181
00:13:36,292 --> 00:13:40,542
and wondered if maybe
one of her kids was gay, too.

182
00:13:42,708 --> 00:13:45,792
So she just went, "Hey, so
I was kind of wondering..."

183
00:13:46,833 --> 00:13:48,917
Pretty much just like that.

184
00:13:49,042 --> 00:13:51,000
I... I see.

185
00:13:53,500 --> 00:13:55,375
Sorry for not telling you sooner.

186
00:13:55,500 --> 00:13:57,375
I should have let you know.

187
00:13:57,500 --> 00:13:59,917
No, it's actually a huge relief.

188
00:14:01,500 --> 00:14:06,792
You always hope the family of
the person you love will accept you.

189
00:14:09,042 --> 00:14:12,333
Oh, and my dad told me this, too.

190
00:14:15,958 --> 00:14:19,833
"Our doors are always open to him."

191
00:14:26,833 --> 00:14:30,683
Is... is that true?

192
00:14:32,250 --> 00:14:33,500
Yeah.

193
00:14:57,632 --> 00:14:59,901
"Aoba Dormitory"

194
00:15:01,528 --> 00:15:04,403
What is with your hair, Sui?

195
00:15:19,958 --> 00:15:22,125
It's nice to meet you. I'm Kishida Sui.

196
00:15:22,217 --> 00:15:23,509
I'm a third year...

197
00:15:24,500 --> 00:15:25,875
Um...

198
00:15:26,292 --> 00:15:29,375
Harutora and I are dating.

199
00:15:29,833 --> 00:15:31,167
Is that so?

200
00:15:31,458 --> 00:15:34,083
I'm Harutora's mom, Aya.

201
00:15:36,250 --> 00:15:36,875
Huh?

202
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:39,917
Are you nervous? How adorable!

203
00:15:44,667 --> 00:15:45,958
She's always like this.

204
00:15:48,333 --> 00:15:49,750
Where are Shogo and the others?

205
00:15:49,875 --> 00:15:51,375
Over there with their dad.

206
00:15:51,500 --> 00:15:54,333
We wouldn't be able to hear
ourselves think if they were here.

207
00:15:54,833 --> 00:15:57,292
By the way, Sui, do you have any siblings?

208
00:15:57,792 --> 00:16:00,042
I'm an only child.

209
00:16:01,250 --> 00:16:02,500
An only child?

210
00:16:03,708 --> 00:16:05,583
Look, it's Harutora!

211
00:16:05,708 --> 00:16:08,292
- Wait for me!
- Who's that guy? He's so handsome!

212
00:16:09,833 --> 00:16:10,833
He's my boyfriend.

213
00:16:10,958 --> 00:16:12,125
Boyfriend...?!

214
00:16:12,250 --> 00:16:13,684
- Quiet down, you two!
- What do you mean, boyfriend?!

215
00:16:13,708 --> 00:16:16,208
Sorry about that. We're a noisy bunch.

216
00:16:16,500 --> 00:16:17,917
Not at all, really.

217
00:16:18,583 --> 00:16:20,833
I don't have any
siblings, so it's really nice.

218
00:16:21,542 --> 00:16:23,167
It feels like having little brothers.

219
00:16:23,292 --> 00:16:25,042
Really?

220
00:16:25,167 --> 00:16:26,583
Since you're an only child,

221
00:16:26,708 --> 00:16:29,500
I was worried all the
racket would bother you.

222
00:16:29,625 --> 00:16:30,875
What a relief.

223
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:36,125
It's always chaotic here,
but you're welcome anytime.

224
00:16:38,083 --> 00:16:39,333
Really?

225
00:16:39,792 --> 00:16:41,875
Truly. Come visit whenever you want.

226
00:16:43,583 --> 00:16:44,792
Thank you.

227
00:16:47,833 --> 00:16:49,167
I definitely will.

228
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:53,417
- All right, sorry about them.
- Everyone, settle down!

229
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:56,417
Come on, behave.

230
00:17:00,917 --> 00:17:02,250
I'm so glad...

231
00:17:11,500 --> 00:17:14,250
Your family is so close and warm.

232
00:17:16,667 --> 00:17:21,292
That was the first time I've
ever seen my mom wear makeup.

233
00:17:22,750 --> 00:17:26,792
She definitely wanted to
make a good impression on you.

234
00:17:33,500 --> 00:17:35,000
It made me really happy.

235
00:17:36,208 --> 00:17:39,292
Having the person you love
introduce you to their family.

236
00:17:42,750 --> 00:17:44,667
Someday, I want to...

237
00:17:45,833 --> 00:17:47,083
What was that?

238
00:17:48,250 --> 00:17:49,500
Nothing.

239
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:55,167
Pardon the intrusion.

240
00:17:55,292 --> 00:17:56,875
[College Counseling Room]

241
00:18:04,208 --> 00:18:06,458
What a relief!

242
00:18:06,833 --> 00:18:09,333
Your teacher said you're on
track to get into your top choice.

243
00:18:09,458 --> 00:18:12,208
It's too early to celebrate, Mom.

244
00:18:13,292 --> 00:18:17,292
By the way, I'd like to say
hello to your roommate.

245
00:18:17,708 --> 00:18:19,208
Ah...

246
00:18:21,917 --> 00:18:24,042
He has practice today, so he isn't here.

247
00:18:24,167 --> 00:18:25,375
I see.

248
00:18:26,167 --> 00:18:27,417
Sui!

249
00:18:28,375 --> 00:18:29,500
Harutora.

250
00:18:30,667 --> 00:18:33,792
Excuse me, are you Sui's mother?

251
00:18:33,917 --> 00:18:35,458
Oh, yes.

252
00:18:36,167 --> 00:18:37,643
Thank you so much for
everything he's done for me.

253
00:18:37,667 --> 00:18:40,167
I'm Kurobe Harutora, a sophomore.

254
00:18:40,292 --> 00:18:41,667
So you're Harutora?

255
00:18:41,792 --> 00:18:43,125
Yes, ma'am.

256
00:18:44,667 --> 00:18:46,208
My, you're tall!

257
00:18:46,333 --> 00:18:48,083
You look like a basketball player.

258
00:18:48,208 --> 00:18:49,750
He actually plays basketball.

259
00:18:50,292 --> 00:18:51,375
I'm so glad.

260
00:18:51,875 --> 00:18:55,958
I've really wanted to meet Sui's mom.

261
00:18:56,083 --> 00:18:59,958
Wait, did you slip away
from practice just for this?

262
00:19:00,083 --> 00:19:01,167
Yes.

263
00:19:01,542 --> 00:19:04,333
Because you're his mother,
and you mean the world to him.

264
00:19:09,042 --> 00:19:15,250
He's always looking out for me,

265
00:19:16,083 --> 00:19:18,417
and I'm truly grateful that I met him.

266
00:19:18,833 --> 00:19:20,000
Is that so?

267
00:19:20,667 --> 00:19:24,250
Please keep looking after him, then.

268
00:19:24,875 --> 00:19:26,000
I will!

269
00:19:28,792 --> 00:19:29,917
- Isn't that nice?
- Yeah.

270
00:19:33,333 --> 00:19:36,292
Harutora is such a wonderful boy.

271
00:19:36,417 --> 00:19:37,250
Yeah.

272
00:19:37,375 --> 00:19:40,292
He's thoughtful and so kind.

273
00:19:41,458 --> 00:19:43,583
Just like the sun.

274
00:19:44,875 --> 00:19:46,542
That's a lovely way to put it.

275
00:19:49,375 --> 00:19:52,958
You seem so much brighter these days, Sui.

276
00:19:53,958 --> 00:19:55,083
What?

277
00:19:56,083 --> 00:19:59,500
Around the end of middle school,

278
00:19:59,625 --> 00:20:02,042
you started locking yourself
in your room all the time.

279
00:20:02,500 --> 00:20:06,500
Then in high school, you suddenly
insisted on moving into the dorms.

280
00:20:07,917 --> 00:20:11,958
That was when I realized
my little boy was growing up so fast.

281
00:20:12,667 --> 00:20:14,167
I felt so lonely.

282
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:19,917
But seeing you now, I'm at peace.

283
00:20:20,292 --> 00:20:22,542
- Mom...
- Oh, by the way,

284
00:20:22,667 --> 00:20:25,125
I ran into Mirai the other day.

285
00:20:26,500 --> 00:20:29,375
Your first crush, remember?

286
00:20:32,458 --> 00:20:33,667
I'm sorry, Mom.

287
00:20:37,875 --> 00:20:45,542
Actually... living at home
used to be agonizing for me.

288
00:20:51,417 --> 00:20:56,042
It hurt so much having
to lie all the time.

289
00:20:57,833 --> 00:20:59,167
Lie?

290
00:21:05,875 --> 00:21:07,167
The truth is...

291
00:21:11,875 --> 00:21:18,917
I'm not attracted to girls.

292
00:21:23,833 --> 00:21:29,375
I hope we can tell the
people around us someday.

293
00:21:29,500 --> 00:21:31,351
[Broke my parents' hearts] [They didn't understand]
It's just that, right now, I'm still a little...

294
00:21:31,375 --> 00:21:33,208
Thank you for telling me.

295
00:21:33,333 --> 00:21:37,250
They just went, "Got it! Congratulations!"

296
00:21:37,375 --> 00:21:42,042
I started to feel like I
should value myself, too.

297
00:21:44,542 --> 00:21:46,333
The truth is...

298
00:21:47,458 --> 00:21:48,708
I'm in love with you.

299
00:21:48,833 --> 00:21:52,542
I hate when people make fun of you.

300
00:21:52,917 --> 00:21:54,333
This smells good.

301
00:21:54,458 --> 00:21:58,208
I love you so much, Sui.

302
00:21:58,792 --> 00:22:02,792
No matter what,
I'll always stay by your side.

303
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:09,167
I like guys.

304
00:22:14,542 --> 00:22:16,458
I'm sorry for hiding it
from you for so long.

305
00:22:17,125 --> 00:22:21,917
But more than anything,
I want you to understand.

306
00:22:22,042 --> 00:22:23,333
So...

307
00:22:29,292 --> 00:22:33,625
It's always chaotic here,
but you're welcome anytime.

308
00:22:35,625 --> 00:22:37,333
You can't be serious...

309
00:23:30,083 --> 00:23:32,208
[Next Episode]

310
00:23:32,333 --> 00:23:34,125
Harutora wouldn't understand.

311
00:23:34,250 --> 00:23:36,250
Right now, we just have
to give him some space.

312
00:23:36,375 --> 00:23:39,917
Better to regret doing
something than to regret never trying.

313
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:43,542
I didn't think you'd come.

314
00:23:43,667 --> 00:23:46,417
I'm sorry, especially when
things are so critical for Harutora.

315
00:23:46,542 --> 00:23:49,542
I want you to be happy.

316
00:23:49,667 --> 00:23:51,627
It's because you gave it
everything you had, Sui.

317
00:23:51,708 --> 00:23:53,833
Ever since I met you,

318
00:23:53,958 --> 00:23:55,833
my life truly began.

319
00:23:55,958 --> 00:23:59,125
[This drama is purely fictional.]
I'm so glad I can be who I am.
